meta {
  name: Preview a graph rebuild
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/graph/rebuild/preview
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
}

docs {
  Sizing + honesty read for `POST /api/graph/rebuild`, so the cost and the limits are known
  before starting the job.

  Returns `{documents, missing_payload, extraction_enabled}`:
  - `documents` — how many documents the rebuild would walk.
  - `missing_payload` — how many of those were ingested before their connector's structural
    claims (ADO dev-links/hierarchy, GitLab MR joins, Jira issue links, Octopus deployments)
    were persisted. A rebuild can ADD to and correct those, but cannot authoritatively
    replace them, so their existing edges are preserved instead. Sync a source once to make
    its documents fully rebuildable.
  - `extraction_enabled` — whether `with_triples=true` is available at all.

  Add `?source_id=azure_devops:TFS` to scope it to one source.
}
